          <item>
           <widget class="QWidget" name="methods_widget" native="true">
            <property name="visible">
             <bool>false</bool>
            </property>
            <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="methods_layout">
             <property name="spacing">
              <number>10</number>
             </property>
             <property name="leftMargin">
              <number>0</number>
             </property>
             <property name="topMargin">
              <number>6</number>
             </property>
             <property name="rightMargin">
              <number>0</number>
             </property>
             <property name="bottomMargin">
              <number>0</number>
             </property>
             <item>
              <widget class="QLabel" name="methods_label">
               <property name="text">
                <string>&lt;b&gt;Variables:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;e&lt;/i&gt; is an event of the expert and &lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt; a detection. True positive (TP): a correct detection (&lt;i&gt;e&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt; are the same). False positive (FP): an incorrect detection (&lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt; does not match any &lt;i&gt;e&lt;/i&gt;). False negative (FN): an event missed (&lt;i&gt;e&lt;/i&gt; not detected).&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Metrics:&lt;/b&gt; precision = TP / (TP + FP), the fraction of the detections that are correct. Recall = TP / (TP + FN), the fraction of the events found. F1 score = 2 × (precision × recall) / (precision + recall). Kappa = 2 (TP × TN − FN × FP) / ((TP + FP)(FP + TN) + (TP + FN)(FN + TN)), in the samples domain only: a conservative agreement, because the expected agreement is removed from the score.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Samples domain:&lt;/b&gt; the events &lt;i&gt;e&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt; are sampled at 100 Hz, so TP, TN, FP and FN are numbers of samples (TP-samples = 500: 500 samples of the expert events are correctly detected). The evaluation is conservative (strict), but many shorter &lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt; can match a longer &lt;i&gt;e&lt;/i&gt; without significant penalty: not suited for event density.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Events domain:&lt;/b&gt; with the Jaccard index, (intersection of &lt;i&gt;e&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt;) / (union of &lt;i&gt;e&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt;). A &lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt; is a TP when its Jaccard index exceeds the threshold, and only one &lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt; can match an &lt;i&gt;e&lt;/i&gt;: the one with the highest Jaccard index. Suited for event density, but the threshold must be defined.</string>
               </property>
               <property name="textFormat">
                <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
               </property>
               <property name="wordWrap">
                <bool>true</bool>
               </property>
               <property name="variant" stdset="0">
                <string notr="true">help</string>
               </property>
              </widget>
             </item>
            </layout>
           </widget>
          </item>
